    "part_notes": "Material: 20MnCrS5 +HL (C≤0.2%) according to ISO 683-3\nwith isothermal annealing (+FP) for micro-structured ferrit-pearlite,\n152-201HB. General tolerance: ISO 22081; ISO 14405. Heat treatment: with isothermal annealing (+FP) for micro-structured ferrit-pearlite, 152-201HB\nLow pressure carburizing and Nitrogen quenching (pressure: 10bars maximum)\nChecking according to standard 400.930.007\n① area without carburizing and quenching\n② area that can be without carburizing and quenching\nSurface hardness: 680-850HV10\nCase depths (CHD0.3/550)\nM1: 0.65 - 1.05mm\nM2: 0.65 - 1.05mm\nM4: 0.35mm minimum\nNo surface burn marks allowed\nCore hardness M3: 320-450HV30 Coating: PASSIVATION OR WATER-SOLUBLE OIL:\nMUST BE COMPATIBLE WITH PROCESS WELDING AND WASHING MACHINES 1. 20MnCrS5 +HL (C≤0.2%) according to ISO 683-3 with isothermal annealing (+FP) for micro-structured ferrit-pearlite, 152-201HB. 2. Low pressure carburizing and Nitrogen quenching (pressure: 10bars maximum). Checking according to standard 400.930.007. ① area without carburizing and quenching; ② area that can be without carburizing and quenching. Surface hardness: 680-850HV10. Case depths (CHD0.3/550): M1: 0.65-1.05mm; M2: 0.65-1.05mm; M4: 0.35mm minimum. No surface burn marks allowed. Core hardness M3: 320-450HV30. Reference G.02.1 is shown alongside the case-depth requirements. 3. UNLESS OTHERWISE SPECIFIED: GENERAL TOLERANCES ACCORDING TO ISO 22081. Position tolerance frame: 0.4 relative to datums A, B, C. ANGLES: ±3°. DIMENSIONS: ±0.25. Surface texture symbols shown in note 3: parenthesized Rz 25 symbol and Rz16 symbol. General edge requirements ACC. TO DIN ISO 13715: external edge symbol with limits -0.1 and -0.3; internal edge symbol with limits +0.3 and +0.1. 4. CONTROL SPECIFICATION: FITTED ON DIAMETER 196.721+/-0.01 AND AXIAL REFERENCE A. CONTROL SPEC USED FOR ALL DIMENSIONS AND HELICAL GEAR DATA EXCEPT INNER DIA 196.6H8 AND H MEASUREMENT. 5. NO BURRS. 6. PASSIVATION OR WATER-SOLUBLE OIL: MUST BE COMPATIBLE WITH PROCESS WELDING AND WASHING MACHINES. 7. DO NOT USE SILICON OILS, GREASE OR SEALANTS. 8. NON MAGNETIZED PARTS. RESIDUAL MAGNETIZATION ≤ 5 Gauss. 9. CLEANLINESS: MUST BE FREE FROM VISIBLE DIRT (E.G. CHIPS, SWARF). THE EXAMINATION SHOULD BE DONE UNDER RATED ILLUMINANCE CONDITIONS OF 750 lux. 10. WET SURFACE: 65847,477mm2. 11. INERTIA: 0,014kgxm2. Characteristic legend: Internal 18, identified by a filled diamond; Internal Followed 0; Customer 0; Customer Followed 0; Safety and/or Regulation 1, identified by the circled inverted-triangle R symbol; Other 0. Material and surface treatment shall be compliant with the latest Valeo BRDS list (Banned, Restricted, Declarable Substance) available in SRM / Reference Documents / Sustainable Development. Compliance confirmation with latest BRDS List is required via IMDS approved report and certified for Initial Sample Validation (ISV). Report shall be reviewed & remained valid for each Yearly Initial Sample (YIS), any modification shall lead to an update in the IMDS Portal. The general-tolerance field beneath the revision table states ISO 14405. WARNING : 3D MODEL IS NOT REPRESENTATIVE AND MUST NOT BE USED FOR THE MACHINING REF: DRAWING NUMBER ASD260020 CREATED BY: AMIT SRIVASTAVA; CREATION DATE: 12-02-2026. Material is specified as SEE NOTES; the referenced material notes are not visible in the supplied crops.",
    "part_level_specs": {
      "general_tolerance_standard": "ISO 22081; ISO 14405",
      "general_notes": [
        {
          "note_text": "1. 20MnCrS5 +HL (C≤0.2%) according to ISO 683-3 with isothermal annealing (+FP) for micro-structured ferrit-pearlite, 152-201HB.",
          "category": "process"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "2. Low pressure carburizing and Nitrogen quenching (pressure: 10bars maximum). Checking according to standard 400.930.007. ① area without carburizing and quenching; ② area that can be without carburizing and quenching. Surface hardness: 680-850HV10. Case depths (CHD0.3/550): M1: 0.65-1.05mm; M2: 0.65-1.05mm; M4: 0.35mm minimum. No surface burn marks allowed. Core hardness M3: 320-450HV30. Reference G.02.1 is shown alongside the case-depth requirements.",
          "category": "process"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "3. UNLESS OTHERWISE SPECIFIED: GENERAL TOLERANCES ACCORDING TO ISO 22081. Position tolerance frame: 0.4 relative to datums A, B, C. ANGLES: ±3°. DIMENSIONS: ±0.25.",
          "category": "tolerance"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "Surface texture symbols shown in note 3: parenthesized Rz 25 symbol and Rz16 symbol.",
          "category": "finish"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "General edge requirements ACC. TO DIN ISO 13715: external edge symbol with limits -0.1 and -0.3; internal edge symbol with limits +0.3 and +0.1.",
          "category": "deburr"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "4. CONTROL SPECIFICATION: FITTED ON DIAMETER 196.721+/-0.01 AND AXIAL REFERENCE A. CONTROL SPEC USED FOR ALL DIMENSIONS AND HELICAL GEAR DATA EXCEPT INNER DIA 196.6H8 AND H MEASUREMENT.",
          "category": "inspection"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "5. NO BURRS.",
          "category": "deburr"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "6. PASSIVATION OR WATER-SOLUBLE OIL: MUST BE COMPATIBLE WITH PROCESS WELDING AND WASHING MACHINES.",
          "category": "finish"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "7. DO NOT USE SILICON OILS, GREASE OR SEALANTS.",
          "category": "process"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "8. NON MAGNETIZED PARTS. RESIDUAL MAGNETIZATION ≤ 5 Gauss.",
          "category": "inspection"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "9. CLEANLINESS: MUST BE FREE FROM VISIBLE DIRT (E.G. CHIPS, SWARF). THE EXAMINATION SHOULD BE DONE UNDER RATED ILLUMINANCE CONDITIONS OF 750 lux.",
          "category": "inspection"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "10. WET SURFACE: 65847,477mm2.",
          "category": "other"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "11. INERTIA: 0,014kgxm2.",
          "category": "other"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "Characteristic legend: Internal 18, identified by a filled diamond; Internal Followed 0; Customer 0; Customer Followed 0; Safety and/or Regulation 1, identified by the circled inverted-triangle R symbol; Other 0.",
          "category": "other"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "Material and surface treatment shall be compliant with the latest Valeo BRDS list (Banned, Restricted, Declarable Substance) available in SRM / Reference Documents / Sustainable Development.",
          "category": "other"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "Compliance confirmation with latest BRDS List is required via IMDS approved report and certified for Initial Sample Validation (ISV). Report shall be reviewed & remained valid for each Yearly Initial Sample (YIS), any modification shall lead to an update in the IMDS Portal.",
          "category": "inspection"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "The general-tolerance field beneath the revision table states ISO 14405.",
          "category": "tolerance"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "WARNING : 3D MODEL IS NOT REPRESENTATIVE AND MUST NOT BE USED FOR THE MACHINING",
          "category": "process"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "REF: DRAWING NUMBER ASD260020",
          "category": "other"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "CREATED BY: AMIT SRIVASTAVA; CREATION DATE: 12-02-2026.",
          "category": "other"
        },
        {
          "note_text": "Material is specified as SEE NOTES; the referenced material notes are not visible in the supplied crops.",
          "category": "other"
        }
      ]
    },
